      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سنّنهُ</span></b> : see 1, near the beginning. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سنّن المَنْطِقَ</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>He made the speech good,</i> or <i>beautiful;</i> (M, L, K;) as though he polished it. (M,
L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سنّن إِلَيْهِ الرُّمْحَ</span>, (M, L, K,) inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَسْنِينٌ</span>, (M, L,) <i>He directed,</i> or <i>pointed, the
spear towards him,</i> or <i>it.</i> (M, L, K.)

